Stock project-load attempt
--------------------------
UI reached:
  LOAD 1 SAMPLE? CONFIRM Y/N
  after SELECT ALL: LOAD 2 SAMPLES? CONFIRM Y/N
Result screen: SAMPLE MEMORY FULL
Upstream meaning: load-done callback's zero-count message, not memory exhaustion.

Firmware hooks (OS 1.53 addresses):
  FUN_400d1680 -> d0 = 0xFFFFFFFF
  FUN_400ec6d2 entry, stack argument 0 -> buffer starts ff ff ff ff 00 00 00 00
  FUN_400d1c90 entry, reference argument -> first word ffffffff
Same result with one marked row and with SELECT ALL. The UI's marked/selected
state does not reach the loader as a valid file reference.

Interpretation
--------------
Live audio model works; stock sample playback does not. The sample is valid on
card and the card indexes are valid. Blocker is the browser-selection to
file-reference handoff (or unresolved browser key behavior), not sample encoding.
OS 1.53 evidence only; no 1.54 execution claim.

No injection, filter/amp sweep, or second-track regression was attempted.
